{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And brought low.</b> From the nifal binyan, like ימס לבב העם (Joshua 7:5), and the meaning: because of this they came to lowliness." "<b>And do not lift up to them.</b> Some say the tav addresses HaShem and its meaning is forgiveness. But what seems right to me is that not one of them has a head or a soul that should be lifted up to them, because the vav functions in the sense equivalent to וישפל, or the word ארץ is elided, as in ולא נשא אותם הארץ (Genesis 13:6). And the grammarian who said that the word אל is found only for a command is incorrect, as testified by ודרך נתיבה אל מות (Proverbs 12:28)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:43.421702959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}